# Installation Guide

## 1. Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/jsm-analyzer.git
cd jsm-analyzer
```

---

## 2. Create Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate environment:

### Windows

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### Linux / macOS

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

---

## 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# Streamlit Secrets Configuration

Create:

```text
.streamlit/secrets.toml
```

Example:

```toml
[jira]
url = "YOUR_JIRA_URL"
email = "YOUR_EMAIL"
api_token = "YOUR_API_TOKEN"

[supabase]
url = "YOUR_SUPABASE_URL"
service_role_key = "YOUR_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"

[auth.users.admin]
password_hash = "YOUR_HASH"
role = "support_admin"
```

---

# Running Locally

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

Application URL:

```text
http://localhost:8501
```

---

# Docker Deployment

## Build and Run

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

---

# Streamlit Cloud Deployment

## Deployment Steps

1. Push project to GitHub
2. Connect GitHub repository to Streamlit Cloud
3. Configure secrets
4. Deploy application

---

# Security Considerations

## Recommended Security Practices

* Keep GitHub repository private
* Never commit secrets.toml
* Rotate Jira API tokens periodically
* Use strong bcrypt password hashes
* Restrict administrative accounts
* Monitor audit logs regularly

